SAK ERP – Windows Server Installation & Deployment Runbook

Version: 1.0
Date: 14-Feb-2026
Audience: Provider Deployment Team + Client IT Team
Target OS: Windows Server 2019 / 2022

====================================================================
1) PURPOSE
====================================================================
This runbook provides exact steps to install and run SAK ERP on a client Windows Server.
It covers:
- Prerequisites
- Runtime installation
- App deployment
- IIS reverse proxy setup
- Service management
- Validation
- Troubleshooting and rollback


====================================================================
2) ARCHITECTURE (WINDOWS)
====================================================================
- Web App (Next.js): localhost:3000
- API App (NestJS): localhost:4000
- Reverse Proxy: IIS (public 80/443) forwarding:
  - /              -> http://127.0.0.1:3000
  - /api/v1/*      -> http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1/*
- Process Manager: PM2


====================================================================
3) PREREQUISITES
====================================================================
3.1 Server
[ ] Windows Server 2019/2022 (updated)
[ ] 4 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, 80+ GB SSD
[ ] Static IP or fixed DNS
[ ] Firewall rules ready: 80, 443, 3389

3.2 Access
[ ] RDP access with local Administrator permissions
[ ] Folder path confirmed (example: C:\apps\sak-erp)

3.3 External Dependencies
[ ] Decide DB mode: Managed Supabase OR Local Self-Hosted Supabase
[ ] If Local Supabase: Docker + WSL2 (or Linux VM) approved by client IT
[ ] Storage configuration (Supabase local object storage/S3/local)
[ ] SMTP/OAuth config for email
[ ] SSL certificate availability (IIS cert or org cert)


====================================================================
4) INSTALL REQUIRED SOFTWARE
====================================================================
Open PowerShell as Administrator.

4.1 Install Node.js LTS 20.x
- Download MSI from official Node.js site and install.
- Verify:
  node -v
  npm -v

4.2 Enable Corepack + PNPM 9.x
  corepack enable
  corepack prepare pnpm@9.0.0 --activate
  pnpm -v

4.3 Install PM2 globally
  npm install -g pm2
  pm2 -v

4.4 Install Git
- Install Git for Windows.
- Verify:
  git --version

4.5 Install IIS + URL Rewrite + ARR
- Enable IIS role from Server Manager.
- Install URL Rewrite module.
- Install Application Request Routing (ARR).
- In IIS Manager, enable Proxy under ARR settings.



4.6 Install Docker + WSL2 (Required for Local Supabase)
- Enable WSL2 and install Ubuntu:
  wsl --install
- Reboot if prompted.
- Install Docker Desktop (or Docker Engine in Linux VM).
- Verify Docker:
  docker --version
  docker compose version

4.7 (Optional but recommended) Install Supabase CLI
  npm install -g supabase
  supabase --version


====================================================================
5) LOCAL SUPABASE SETUP (SELF-HOSTED ON WINDOWS SERVER)
====================================================================
If client wants local database + auth + storage, use this section.

5.1 Clone Supabase self-host stack
  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path C:\apps\supabase -Force
  Set-Location C:\apps\supabase
  git clone https://github.com/supabase/supabase .
  Set-Location .\docker

5.2 Prepare configuration
  Copy-Item .env.example .env
- Edit `.env` and set strong secrets/passwords:
  [ ] POSTGRES_PASSWORD
  [ ] JWT_SECRET
  [ ] ANON_KEY
  [ ] SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
  [ ] SMTP settings (if using local auth email)

5.3 Start Supabase services
  docker compose pull
  docker compose up -d
  docker compose ps

5.4 Validate local Supabase endpoints
- API gateway: http://127.0.0.1:8000
- Postgres (inside stack, commonly mapped to 5432/54322 depending config)
- Studio: http://127.0.0.1:3000 (if enabled in compose)

5.5 Save values for SAK ERP env
- SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
- SUPABASE_KEY=<SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from Supabase .env>

Note:
- For production reliability on Windows Server, hosting Supabase in a dedicated Linux VM is preferred over long-term Docker Desktop usage.

====================================================================
5) DEPLOY APPLICATION FILES
6) DEPLOY APPLICATION FILES
5.1 Prepare directory
6.1 Prepare directory
  Set-Location C:\apps\sak-erp

5.2 Get source/artifact
6.2 Get source/artifact
  git clone <your_repo_url> .

Option B: Copy artifact zip/tar and extract into C:\apps\sak-erp

5.3 Install dependencies
6.3 Install dependencies

5.4 Build apps
6.4 Build apps
  pnpm -C apps/web build


====================================================================
6) CONFIGURE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
7) CONFIGURE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
Create env files with production values:

6.1 API env file
7.1 API env file
Minimum typical keys:
- NODE_ENV=production
- PORT=4000
- SUPABASE_URL=...
- SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000   (for local Supabase)
- SUPABASE_KEY=<SERVICE_ROLE_KEY>      (from local Supabase .env)
- JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=...
- EMAIL_* (if SMTP/OAuth used)

6.2 Web env file
7.2 Web env file
Minimum typical keys:
- NODE_ENV=production
- NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/api/v1
- INTERNAL_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1

Security Note:
- Do not share secrets over email/chat.
- Restrict file permissions to admin/deployment users only.


====================================================================
8) DATABASE MIGRATIONS
====================================================================
Run required migrations/scripts in approved order.
Examples (project-specific):
- SQL scripts provided by release package
- Prisma generate/migrate if applicable

If using Local Supabase Postgres:
- Run SQL scripts against Supabase Postgres database (via psql/Studio/SQL editor).
- Confirm all required tables/functions/views are present before app start.

If using Prisma generation:
  Set-Location C:\apps\sak-erp\packages\database
  pnpm exec prisma generate --schema prisma\schema.prisma


====================================================================
9) START SERVICES WITH PM2
====================================================================
From C:\apps\sak-erp:

9.1 Start API
  pm2 start npm --name sak-api --cwd C:\apps\sak-erp\apps\api -- run start:prod

9.2 Start Web
  pm2 start node_modules\next\dist\bin\next --name sak-web --cwd C:\apps\sak-erp\apps\web -- start -p 3000

9.3 Verify process list
  pm2 list

9.4 Save PM2 process state
  pm2 save

9.5 Configure startup after reboot (Windows)
Recommended options:
- Use PM2 startup helper for Windows if available in environment
- OR create Scheduled Task at startup that runs:
    pm2 resurrect

(If using Scheduled Task, run it with highest privileges under service account.)


====================================================================
10) CONFIGURE IIS REVERSE PROXY
====================================================================
10.1 Create/choose IIS Site
- Bind host/domain and ports 80/443.
- Attach SSL certificate for 443.

10.2 URL Rewrite rules
Rule 1: API
- Match URL: ^api/v1/(.*)
- Rewrite to: http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1/{R:1}

Rule 2: Web
- Match URL: (.*)
- Rewrite to: http://127.0.0.1:3000/{R:1}

10.3 Enable proxy features
- In ARR Server Proxy Settings: Enable Proxy.
- Preserve host header if required by app behavior.

10.4 Optional hardening
- Add HTTP -> HTTPS redirect.
- Add security headers (HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, etc.).


====================================================================
11) GO-LIVE VALIDATION CHECKS
====================================================================
11.1 Service-level checks
  pm2 list
  pm2 logs sak-api --lines 100
  pm2 logs sak-web --lines 100

11.2 Local endpoint checks (on server)
  curl http://127.0.0.1:3000/
  curl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1
  curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/rest/v1/

11.3 Public URL checks
- Open application URL in browser.
- Login with admin user.
- Verify key workflows:
  [ ] Purchase Requisition create
  [ ] Smart Job Order create/preview
  [ ] Complete Job Order flow
  [ ] UID traceability view
  [ ] Email action (if configured)


====================================================================
12) OPERATIONS (DAY-2)
====================================================================
12.1 Common PM2 commands
  pm2 list
  pm2 restart sak-api
  pm2 restart sak-web
  pm2 stop sak-api
  pm2 stop sak-web
  pm2 logs sak-api --lines 200
  pm2 logs sak-web --lines 200

12.2 App update process
1. Backup DB and env files.
2. Pull/copy new release.
3. Install deps and build.
4. Restart PM2 processes.
5. Smoke test critical flows.

12.3 Backup expectations
- Daily DB backup
- Weekly restore test (non-prod)
- Keep app artifact for rollback

12.4 Local Supabase backup commands (example)
- Logical backup:
  docker exec -t supabase-db pg_dump -U postgres -d postgres > C:\backups\sakerp_YYYYMMDD.sql
- Restore (planned window):
  type C:\backups\sakerp_YYYYMMDD.sql | docker exec -i supabase-db psql -U postgres -d postgres


====================================================================
13) TROUBLESHOOTING QUICK GUIDE
====================================================================
Issue: App not reachable on domain
- Check IIS site bindings (host/port/cert)
- Check URL Rewrite rules
- Check Windows Firewall ports

Issue: API 500/permission errors
- Check API env values
- Check role/permission data in DB
- Check PM2 logs for stack trace

Issue: Supabase local services not available
- Check Docker daemon is running
- Run `docker compose ps` in Supabase docker folder
- Check container logs (`docker compose logs -f`)
- Confirm app uses correct `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_KEY`

Issue: Web loads but API fails
- Confirm reverse proxy route /api/v1 -> 4000
- Confirm API process is running
- Confirm NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is /api/v1

Issue: PM2 not restoring on reboot
- Validate startup task/service account permissions
- Test `pm2 resurrect` manually


====================================================================
14) ROLLBACK PROCEDURE
====================================================================
1. Stop current processes:
   pm2 stop sak-api
   pm2 stop sak-web
2. Restore previous app artifact/build.
3. Restore previous DB backup if schema/data changed.
4. Start previous version:
   pm2 start sak-api
   pm2 start sak-web
5. Validate login + 2 critical business flows.


